source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Rename a workspace for all its members.
Every member sees the new name, so it needs -y; without it only the dry run is shown.

USAGE
  holst workspace rename <ws> <name> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  ws     The workspace: id or part of its name
  name   The new name

FLAGS
  -y, --yes       Confirm a risky change; without it only the dry run is shown (exit code 77)
  -n, --dry-run   Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst ws rename easy "Easy design" -y
  $ holst ws rename Easy "Easy design" -n

LEARN MORE
  How a workspace is given: `holst ws -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
